<title>USA: Oakland council members slam cost overruns.</title>
<headline>Oakland council members slam cost overruns.</headline>
<dateline>OAKLAND, California 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oakland city council members on Thursday criticised city, county and coliseum staff for not keeping them well informed about cost overruns and other problems with the Oakland coliseum renovation.</p>
<p>For months, the deal that brought the Raiders football team back to Oakland has been marred by financial and operational problems, drawing fire from public officials.</p>
<p>City officials warned on Thursday that there could be a shortfall in 1998-99 in the joint powers' authority that runs the coliseum if Raiders' ticket sales did not improve.</p>
</text>
